<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.70 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.70 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Cotton Export Corporation of Pakistan (CEC) said on Saturday 1996/97 (July-June) cotton output had reached a provisional 8.707 million 375-lb bales, down from 9.904 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales (year-ago):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.631 (8.150)  2.075 (1.754)  8.707 (9.904)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.595 (8.138)  2.068 (1.733)  8.663 (9.872)</p>
<p> Mill sales     5.612 (6.631)  1.855 (1.243)  7.467 (7.874)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.007 (1.019)  0.002 (0.426)  0.009 (1.446)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   1.011 (0.499)  0.218 (0.083)  1.230 (0.583)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
